;; M4S struct diamond with tail (docs/m4s-contract.md, required fixtures):
;; the m4t_diamond shape with a pair-style CONSTRUCTED head -- spath rows
;; are struct instances of pnode, so the closure's identity rides the
;; intern dictionary.  With edges 1-2, 2-4, 1-3, 3-4, 4-5 fed through the
;; overlay API the closure is nine rows:
;;   spath = { (1,2) (2,4) (1,3) (3,4) (4,5)     copies, nonrec 1 each
;;             (1,4)  rec 2   via 1-2-4 AND 1-3-4
;;             (2,5)  rec 1   via 2-4-5
;;             (3,5)  rec 1   via 3-4-5
;;             (1,5)  rec 1   via (1,4)+(4,5) }
;; and pnode interns the same nine contents with the same support words
;; (each firing supports the constructed pnode row and the spath row with
;; equal multiplicity -- constructor coupling).
;;
;; Deleting edge(1,2) removes exactly spath/pnode (1,2):
;;   (1,4) survives on the 1-3-4 route (rec 2 -> 1), (1,5) survives
;;   through it (rec 1), everything else keeps its support:
;;   spath = 8 rows, pnode = 8 live ids + 1 tombstone.

table (edge int int)
struct (pnode int int)
table (spath pnode)

rule
(edge X Y)
-->
(spath (pnode X Y))

rule
(spath (pnode X Y))
(edge Y Z)
-->
(spath (pnode X Z))
